    "source": "Kilauea Light 2008",
    "description": "KAUAI, Hawaii) -- Kilauea Lighthouse is seen from a designated lookout point, Wednesday, Oct. 29, 2008. Kilauea Lighthouse has been a beacon for mariners since 1913. It served as a pivotal navigation aid for ships sailing on the Orient run. The historic light station consists of a concrete lighthouse, three field stone keepers' quarters, a fuel oil shed, cisterns, and a supply-landing platform. It is one of the nation's most intact historic light stations.",
